  "><span>Request For Map Data Brief</span></button></div></div></div><div class="hidden lg:flex absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 items-center justify-center w-[55%] md:w-[50%] p-10 md:p-6 lg:w-[55%] xl:w-[50%] 2xl:w-[45%] lg:p-8 xl:p-8 2xl:p-14"><img alt="SemiBanner Image" title="SemiBanner Image" width="0" height="0" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class=" w-full object-contain object-right z-1 xl:max-w-full mx-auto lg:h-full" style="color:transparent" sizes="100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.foxsuite.ai%2Fmedia%2Fsumit_royfdfdd%2528699e%2529%2Fedx%2528699e%2529%2Fsites%2Fimage_15.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div></section></div><div id="FAQ"><section class="py-14  "><div class="container mx-auto   lg:px-12 xl:px-0 max-w-7xl"><div class="text-center  mb-16"><h4 class="text-sm leading-none tracking-[0.3em] text-center uppercase text-primary-orange mb-4">Map Data: FAQs</h4><h2 class="mt-3 font-light text-3xl lg:text-[40px] leading-tight text-center text-primary-blue xl:max-w-5xl mx-auto mb-6">Technical and operational considerations that engineers raise before committing to new mapping datasets.</h2></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6  lg:px-12 xl:px-0 max-w-7xl"><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">1. How does US resolution compare to international coverage options?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">US coverage includes 5m hybrid clutter and 10m terrain datasets designed for detailed urban and suburban propagation studies. Outside the US, 30m terrain and clutter datasets are available globally. This structure supports high-precision domestic deployments while enabling immediate access for international feasibility assessments and RFP driven planning.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">2. Can data be purchased only for defined service areas?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 -rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. Data can be acquired for specific service areas rather than entire geographic tiles. This allows teams to align dataset investment with project scope, control OPEX, and support short-term studies or competitive bid responses without committing to unnecessary coverage.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">3. Is external sourcing or file conversion required before use?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 -rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">No. Map Sync allows engineers to select service areas and download terrain and clutter datasets directly within the planning environment. There is no requirement to manually source, reformat, or convert files before using them in active RF studies.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">4. How are terrain and clutter files managed within a project?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 -rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Engineers can define geographic boundaries inside the study grid to control which terrain and clutter files are used. Activating only relevant datasets reduces processing overhead and maintains performance during coverage, interference, and capacity analysis.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">5. Are dataset updates handled manually after subscription?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 -rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Once subscribed, users receive automatic dataset updates. This ensures ongoing projects continue using current terrain and land use references, helping maintain the integrity of propagation modeling data as environmental conditions evolve.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-primary-blue/20 py-6"><button class="w-full flex justify-between items-center gap-5 text-left"><h4 class="text-sm lg:text-lg font-medium text-primary-blue">6. Can engineers continue working while the datasets download?</h4><span class="text-primary-blue text-xl relative w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-100 rotate-0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="absolute transition-all duration-300 opacity-0 -rotate-90" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg></span></button><div style="height:0" class="overflow-hidden transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out"><div class="pt-4"><p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. After initiating downloads through Map Sync, engineers can continue modeling and analysis tasks while terrain and clutter datasets transfer in the background. Once complete, the data becomes available for both new and existing projects without interrupting workflow.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section></div><div id="askAQuestion"><section class="py-14 bg-[#F2F2FF]"><div class="container mx-auto"><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 items-center gap-12 lg:gap-12 "><div class="b w-full"><h4 class="text-sm leading-none tracking-[0.3em] text-start uppercase text-primary-orange">KEY BENEFITS</h4><h2 class="mt-3 font-light text-3xl lg:text-[40px] leading-tight text-start text-primary-blue">Ask a question</h2><p class="mt-3 font-normal lg:text-[14px] max-w-full lg:max-w-[70%] xl:max-w-[80%] 2xl:max-w-[70%] leading-[19.7px] text-start text-gray-600">Talk to one of our experts to answer your questions and get a demo of  Ativa Net with no strings attached. Submit your contact details and we will get back to you shortly.</p><p class="mt-3 lg:text-[14px] max-w-full lg:max-w-[70%] xl:max-w-[80%] 2xl:max-w-[70%] text-start text-gray-600 font-medium text-[14px] leading-[150%] trac